{{!--
    One row of the Spaceship sidebar's equipped-weapons list (#17): name, icon, and damage for a
    single equipped weapon, below the damage-thresholds section (`templates/actors/spaceship/
    sidebar.hbs`). Mirrors the fields daggerheart's own character sidebar shows for an equipped
    item - `templates/sheets/actors/character/sidebar.hbs`'s `.equipment-section`, rendered
    through its own `inventory-item-compact.hbs`.

    Markup/classes are copied by value from that partial - `inventory-item`/
    `inventory-item-compact`/`img-portait`/`item-name`/`item-labels`/`label` are all styled
    unscoped under `.application.daggerheart.dh-style` (`daggerheart.css`), so they render
    identically here for free, same reasoning as `inventory-item.hbs`'s own header comment.

    Read-only by design (no equip toggle, no context menu): this list mirrors the Inventory tab's
    equip state rather than managing it, the same one-way relationship Shield and the damage
    thresholds already have to the equipped armor item. The portrait still opens the weapon's own
    sheet (`editItem`, already wired on this sheet) so the row isn't a dead end.

    Registered as `dhscifi.equipped-weapon` in `src/main.ts`.

    Parameters:
    - weapon {EquippedWeaponRow} : `{uuid, name, img, labels}` - built in
      `spaceship-actor-sheet.ts`'s `#buildEquippedWeapons`. `labels` is the weapon's own
      `_getLabels()` array (trait/range short forms plus damage, `daggerheart` `Item`-level, not
      sheet code) - a plain string, or `{value, icons}` for the damage entry's damage-type chips.
--}}
<li class="inventory-item inventory-item-compact" data-item-uuid="{{weapon.uuid}}">
    <div class="img-portait" data-action="editItem" data-tooltip="{{localize 'DHSCIFI.Rows.EditItem'}}">
        <img src="{{weapon.img}}" class="item-img" alt="{{weapon.name}}" />
    </div>

    <span class="item-name">{{weapon.name}}</span>

    <div class="item-labels">
        <div class="label">
            {{#each weapon.labels as |label|}}
                {{#if label.value}}{{label.value}}{{else}}{{label}}{{/if}}
                {{#each label.icons as |icon|}}
                    <i class="fa-solid {{icon}}"></i>
                {{/each}}
                {{#unless @last}}
                    <span>-</span>
                {{/unless}}
            {{/each}}
        </div>
    </div>
</li>
